// Somebody's own tools, and the reason their hour of mending is worth
// more than anybody else's.
//
// **It buys hit points, not time.** A shift of repair takes exactly as
// long with the kit as without, and costs poles in proportion to what it
// mends — so this makes a person's hour more valuable rather than making
// repair cheap. The tower still pays the same poles per point; it just
// gets more points out of the same day.
//
// Half again, matching `manned_work_pct`, because both answer the same
// question — what is one person's day worth when you have spent
// something on it — and two different numbers for that would be two
// different answers to one design idea.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
ItemDef(
    id: "item.menders_kit",
    name: "Mender's kit",
    glyph: "🧰",
    order: 42,
    kit: KitDef(
        mend_pct: 150,
    ),
)
